# Last match wins, so the blanket rules come first and the per-path pins below override them.

# Text normalisation is declared here rather than inherited from whatever core.autocrlf each
# clone happens to set. The index is ALREADY LF - 1597 of 1598 tracked .cpp/.h/.cs blobs, the
# lone exception being Source/PinWright/Private/Tests/Assets/TestCreateBlendSpaceAxisConfig.cpp -
# so this records the shape the repo is already in; it does not propose a new one. The working
# tree stays mixed on purpose: git checks files out CRLF on Windows, agent editors write LF, and
# NO renormalisation pass was run (see docs/lessons.md). Scripted edits must therefore read a
# file's existing newlines rather than assume either style.
* text=auto

# Binaries, so text=auto's content heuristic never gets a vote on them. Resources/Icon128.png is
# the only one tracked today; the rest are here so a file that lands later cannot be mangled
# before anyone notices. Unreal content assets go through Git LFS in the HOST project
# (../../.gitattributes) - the plugin tracks none, and the LFS filters are deliberately not
# mirrored here, only the "never treat as text" half.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.bmp binary
*.ico binary
*.tga binary
*.dds binary
*.exr binary
*.hdr binary
*.psd binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ogg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.7z binary
*.gz binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.lib binary
*.pdb binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.uasset binary
*.umap binary
*.upk binary
*.udk binary

# mcp-instructions.md is a byte-exact contract, not prose: the `initialize` handshake text is
# duplicated as a C++ literal (Transport/McpRequestCore.cpp) and a Python literal
# (Content/Python/mcp_proxy.py), and both sync guards compare the file's bytes against those
# literals. With core.autocrlf on, a Windows checkout rewrote its newlines to CRLF while the
# literals stay \n, so PinWright.infra.request_core.Initialize failed on every such clone for a
# difference no author could see. Pin the working-tree newlines instead of teaching each guard to
# normalise, which would also hide real CRLF drift creeping into the literals.
mcp-instructions.md text eol=lf

# .pwmodel is source text with a grammar, not prose, and `model.format` will eventually write
# whole files here. Declaring `text` explicitly takes the content heuristic in `* text=auto` out
# of the decision, so the index shape is fixed before an emitter starts producing them. eol is
# deliberately NOT pinned, unlike the entry above: the emitter's contract is to reproduce
# the newline style of the file it rewrote (docs/pwmodel-emitter-and-migration.md), and
# pinning eol=lf would force a renormalising checkout on Windows, which this repo has never run
# (see the blanket note at the top).
*.pwmodel text
